### Layer 3 — Multi-Component Adaptive Momentum

Rather than relying on a single momentum measure (which ALL retail indicators do), NMC blends **four momentum components** with optimized weights:

| Component | Weight | What it Measures |
|---|---|---|
| **Rate of Change (ROC)** | 35% | Raw momentum: how far price has moved |
| **RSI (centered)** | 30% | Mean-reversion pressure: overbought/oversold |
| **Stochastic (centered)** | 20% | Relative position within recent range |
| **Acceleration** | 15% | 2nd derivative: is momentum speeding up or slowing down? |

**Why blend?** Each component captures a different DIMENSION of momentum:
- ROC captures **magnitude** but is noisy
- RSI captures **exhaustion** but can stay extreme in strong trends
- Stochastic captures **range position** but whipsaws in trends
- Acceleration captures **inflection points** but is very noisy alone

Together they create a **360° view of momentum** that no single oscillator can provide.

