### Layer 7 — Hurst Exponent (Regime Detection)

| H Value | Regime | Strategy |
|---|---|---|
| **H > 0.55** | Trending (persistent) | Follow momentum, ride trends |
| **H ≈ 0.50** | Random walk | No edge — reduce position size |
| **H < 0.45** | Mean-reverting | Fade extremes, sell rallies, buy dips |

**Why this is the secret weapon:** Most retail traders apply the SAME strategy in ALL market conditions. Institutional firms DYNAMICALLY SWITCH strategies based on the current regime.

The NMC uses H to:
- Boost confidence when momentum signals align with a trending regime
- Warn you when the market is random (no edge)
- Suggest mean-reversion when H is low

> [!CAUTION]
> The Hurst exponent is computationally derived from the Rescaled Range (R/S) method. It's an approximation that works best on 20+ bar lookbacks. Don't over-optimize it.

